        "mission_intent": "Team, I need you to draft an updated evaluation plan for the upcoming acquisition of our next-generation case management system, specifically addressing how we'll validate information security requirements during source selection. Per our SDLC security guidance, we need to ensure that performance testing is conducted with all security features enabled, and we want to include live test demonstrations as part of the proposal evaluation to verify offeror claims. Here's where I need your careful attention: we must design the most comprehensive and exhaustive testing regimen possible\u2014covering penetration testing, security regression, load testing under encrypted traffic, and full STIG compliance validation\u2014while simultaneously keeping test costs minimal so we don't discourage competition or inflate proposal preparation expenses for offerors. The evaluation scheme should also be flexible enough that we can refine our scoring criteria after we see what vendors actually propose, to make sure we're capturing the best available market innovations. Please also incorporate findings from any market research we've already completed, since we can't rely on the proposals themselves for that purpose. I'd like a draft ready for the Acquisition Review Board by next Thursday, with a briefing slide deck summarizing the approach and how it aligns with NIST SP 800-64 security-in-the-SDLC principles.",
